<xml>
  <block type="device_lcd" x="25" y="25">
    <mutation uid="lcd64" />
    <field name="NAME">display</field>
    <field name="ADDR">0x27</field>
    <field name="COLS">20</field>
    <field name="ROWS">4</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="480" h="240">Purpose: Prepare an 80-byte LCD character grid in RAM, then send the finished 20×4 frame once. Legacy text mode treats zero as a space.
Wiring: HD44780 I2C LCD: address 0x27; I2C SDA A4, SCL A5. Common GND; use each module’s required supply.
Try: Change characters in the frame array, then send the complete frame.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_array_declare" x="385" y="25">
    <field name="VAR">frame</field>
    <field name="TYPE">char</field>
    <field name="SIZE">4,20</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">The whole buffer is allocated once. Shape is rows,columns; cells initially contain zero. Modify cells in RAM, then send the complete buffer.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_typed_variable" x="745" y="25">
    <field name="VAR">phase</field>
    <field name="TYPE">uint8_t</field>
    <value name="VALUE">
      <block type="math_number">
        <field name="NUM">0</field>
      </block>
    </value>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create phase as uint8_t. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_loop_section" x="25" y="180">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="controls_for">
        <field name="VAR">row</field>
        <value name="FROM">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">0</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <value name="TO">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">3</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <value name="BY">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">1</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <statement name="DO">
          <block type="controls_for">
            <field name="VAR">column</field>
            <value name="FROM">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">0</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <value name="TO">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">19</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <value name="BY">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">1</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <statement name="DO">
              <block type="arduino_array_set">
                <mutation rank="2" />
                <field name="VAR">frame</field>
                <value name="INDEX">
                  <block type="variables_get">
                    <field name="VAR">row</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="INDEX2">
                  <block type="variables_get">
                    <field name="VAR">column</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="VALUE">
                  <block type="math_arithmetic">
                    <field name="OP">ADD</field>
                    <value name="A">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">65</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="B">
                      <block type="math_modulo">
                        <value name="DIVIDEND">
                          <block type="math_arithmetic">
                            <field name="OP">ADD</field>
                            <value name="A">
                              <block type="math_arithmetic">
                                <field name="OP">ADD</field>
                                <value name="A">
                                  <block type="variables_get">
                                    <field name="VAR">column</field>
                                  </block>
                                </value>
                                <value name="B">
                                  <block type="variables_get">
                                    <field name="VAR">row</field>
                                  </block>
                                </value>
                              </block>
                            </value>
                            <value name="B">
                              <block type="variables_get">
                                <field name="VAR">phase</field>
                              </block>
                            </value>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <value name="DIVISOR">
                          <block type="math_number">
                            <field name="NUM">26</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Keep the remainder after division. This is useful for wrapping a counter or animation position back to the beginning.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Replace one array element at the given indices. Indices start at zero and must stay below each declared dimension. Other elements keep their previous values.</comment>
              </block>
            </statement>
            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Visit each column from 0 to 19. Indices start at zero; the last index is one less than the size.</comment>
          </block>
        </statement>
        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Visit each row from 0 to 3. Indices start at zero; the last index is one less than the size.</comment>
        <next>
          <block type="device_lcd_buffer">
            <field name="DEVICE">lcd64</field>
            <field name="LAYOUT">YX</field>
            <value name="BUFFER">
              <block type="arduino_array_ref">
                <field name="VAR">frame</field>
                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Pass the entire declared array to the next operation, without making another framebuffer. The receiving block determines the pixel/character format and layout.</comment>
              </block>
            </value>
            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Only now send the prepared array. The loop above changes memory, not the physical output. This action reuses the named device and its wiring.</comment>
            <next>
              <block type="variables_set">
                <field name="VAR">phase</field>
                <value name="VALUE">
                  <block type="math_modulo">
                    <value name="DIVIDEND">
                      <block type="math_arithmetic">
                        <field name="OP">ADD</field>
                        <value name="A">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">phase</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <value name="B">
                          <block type="math_number">
                            <field name="NUM">1</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="DIVISOR">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">26</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Keep the remainder after division. This is useful for wrapping a counter or animation position back to the beginning.</comment>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <next>
                  <block type="base_delay">
                    <value name="DELAY_TIME">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">160</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Wait for the given number of milliseconds (1000 ms = 1 second). This pauses the main program; avoid long waits when loop must service motors, music files or serial input.</comment>
                  </block>
                </next>
              </block>
            </next>
          </block>
        </next>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Build 80 character codes in RAM, then send the 20×4 frame. 65 is ASCII A. Change the arithmetic to design another animation; writing the array alone does not touch the LCD.</comment>
  </block>
</xml>
